# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Disc Caddy marketing page.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version added to dependencies)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Analytics Configuration
**Modified: `app/layout.tsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout's body section, placed after the `<Providers>` component

## Implementation Details

This implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Next.js App Router projects:
- The Analytics component was fetched from the latest Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart)
- The component is placed in the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) to ensure analytics tracking across all pages
- The component is positioned at the end of the body tag, following Next.js best practices
- The existing code structure was preserved with minimal, targeted changes

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linting passed with no issues
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ No breaking changes to existing functionality

## Next Steps

To activate Web Analytics:
1. Deploy this application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
3. Data collection will begin automatically after deployment

The Analytics component will automatically start tracking page views and web vitals once deployed to Vercel.
